{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Elohim came to Balaam.</b> This revelation was for the honor of Israel, for so we find that the Shekhinah was revealed to ordinary people for the sake of the righteous, in the manner of what is said (Genesis 31:24): ״ויבא אלהים אל לבן הארמי בחלום הלילה״, and likewise (ibid. 20): ״ויבא אלהים אל אבימלך״." "<b>And He said, Who are these men with you?</b> We do not find in all the verses that the Holy One, blessed be He, asks except of the wicked — of those whom He wishes to mislead, in order to destroy and annihilate them forever, in the manner of what is written (Job 12:23): ״משגיא לגוים ויאבדם״. And this is what is written of Cain (Genesis 4:9): ״אי הבל אחיך״ — because he denied providence and said 'there is no judgment and there is no Judge and there is no world to come,' He wished to mislead him by asking him as one who does not know. And so too here with Balaam, He wished to ask him in order to mislead him, so that he would say: sometimes He knows and sometimes He does not know." "<b>And so</b> they said in the Midrash (Proverbs 28:10–11): ״משגה רשעים בדרך רע בשחותו הוא יפול ותמימים ינחלו טוב״ — this is Balaam the wicked. For at first the creatures were fenced off from forbidden sexual relations, as is said (Genesis 29:9): ״ורחל באה עם הצאן אשר לאביה״, and it is written (Exodus 2:16): ״ולכהן מדין שבע בנות״. Balaam arose and misled the creatures in forbidden sexual relations — ״בשחותו הוא יפול״: just as he misled the creatures, so the Holy One, blessed be He, misled him and said to him, ״Who are these men with you?״ That wicked one said: there are times when He does not know; so I too will do to His sons whatever I please."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {2 "The heading משלי כ״ח:י׳-י״א appears to cite verses 10–11; the comment bundles the midrashic reading of v. 10 with the phrase ותמימים ינחלו טוב from v. 10b (or the opening of v. 11 in some numbering traditions). Translated the prooftexts as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:03.222689232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}